Package: PArallax
Type: Package
Title: Connectivity Mapping with Depth from Gene and Pathway Perspectives
Version: 1.1.0
Authors@R: person(given = "Sung Young", family = "Kim", role = c("aut", "cre"), email = "palelamp@kku.ac.kr",
                  comment = "School of Medicine, Konkuk University, South Korea")
Description: Ranks library compounds (for example 'LINCS' L1000 signatures) against a
    query signature with the weighted connectivity score (WTCS) computed twice: on
    genes (G) and on pathways (P), after the query and the library are both mapped
    to single-sample pathway scores (seven mapping methods; one pathway database at
    a time). G stays the base ranking and P adds evidence. Compounds are placed in
    tiers, each with the pathways that connect it to the query, and drawn as a ranked
    list and a one-page case figure. No pathway or compound data are shipped: 'KEGG'
    pathways are downloaded from the 'KEGG' REST API, other databases with 'msigdbr',
    and compound information comes from 'signatureSearch' or the user's own table.
    The connectivity score follows Lamb et al. (2006) <doi:10.1126/science.1132939>
    and Subramanian et al. (2017) <doi:10.1016/j.cell.2017.10.049>.
URL: https://github.com/centromics/PArallax
BugReports: https://github.com/centromics/PArallax/issues
License: GPL-3
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: stats, utils, grid, grDevices, ggplot2 (>= 3.4.0), ggrepel, scales, gridExtra, withr
Suggests: GSVA, AnnotationDbi, org.Hs.eg.db, GSEABase, msigdbr, signatureSearch, testthat (>= 3.0.0)
Config/testthat/edition: 3
